run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-watchlist/wl-wrong-belief+governor@6000-01
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Add a button that clears every movie whose `seen` flag is true from the watchlist.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (The request's 'seen' flag maps to the existing WatchItem.watched boolean (the only seen/watched concept in the codebase). Cleanest design: one new store operation WatchlistStore.clearWatched() plus a button on the watchlist page that calls it, disabled via the disabled attribute when watchedCount() === 0. The watchlist owner is explicitly told about the new store method so the parallel owners agree on the cross-unit contract.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (tsc is clean and all owner tests pass; the 2 failures are harness errors in my acceptance test (no router providers for the RouterLink directive in the watchlist template). I replace the watchlist acceptance test with a correctly configured one, restating the unchanged contract so the owner only changes code if the now-runnable test reveals a real gap.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc exit 0, 42/42 tests pass). The acceptance tests confirm the requested behaviour end-to-end: the watchlist page shows a clear-watched button, disabled when nothing is watched, and clicking it removes every watched movie via WatchlistStore.clearWatched(), leaving only unwatched items and resetting watchedCount to 0.)

